recipe|silver-tongue-oil|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The oil separates and refuses to blend. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|simple-pendant|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You wrap the polished stone in a cradle of copper wire and shape a hanging loop. A simple pendant!</ansi>
recipe|simple-pendant|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The stone slips free of the wire cage and cracks on the bench. The materials are ruined.</ansi>
recipe|skitter-shell-bracer|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You pierce each shell, overlap them like scales, and lace them onto a leather backing with copper wire. A skitter-shell bracer!</ansi>
recipe|skitter-shell-bracer|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The brittle shells crack under the awl one after another. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-copper-ore|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You melt the copper out of the rock and pour a small red ingot.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-copper-ore|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The melt slags over. The ore is wasted.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-gold-ore|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You melt the gold from the quartz and pour a small, heavy ingot.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-gold-ore|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The gold runs into the slag and is lost.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-iron-ore|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You bed the ore in the coals and work the bellows until slag runs off and a rough bar of iron is left behind. An iron ingot!</ansi>
recipe|smelt-iron-ore|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The fire never gets hot enough, and the ore crumbles into useless slag.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-silver-ore|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You smelt the silver out over a hot coal fire and pour a bright ingot.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-silver-ore|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The silver burns off in the slag. The ore is wasted.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-tin-ore|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You melt the tin out of the rock and pour a pale ingot.</ansi>
recipe|smelt-tin-ore|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The melt slags over. The ore is wasted.</ansi>
recipe|smoke-meat|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You salt the meat and hang it in the smoke until it turns dark and dry. Smoked meat!</ansi>
recipe|smoke-meat|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The fire flares and chars the meat to cinders.</ansi>
recipe|spatial-stitching|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You bind the setting's hollow into the paste and coax it to hold more than its size should allow. Spatial stitching!</ansi>
recipe|spatial-stitching|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The binding folds in on itself and the enchantment collapses inward. The materials are lost.</ansi>
recipe|spiced-wine|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You mull the herbs and salt into a dark, warming wine. Spiced wine!</ansi>
recipe|spiced-wine|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The mixture ferments wrong and turns to vinegar. The materials are lost.</ansi>
recipe|split-staves|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You split the log along the grain into two clean staves. Bow staves!</ansi>
recipe|split-staves|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The split runs out of the grain and the staves are ruined.</ansi>
recipe|spore-mantle|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">Luminous spores bloom across the pauldrons, forming a living ward. Magic crackles and dies against the fungal barrier.</ansi>
recipe|spore-mantle|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The spores fail to take root. The materials crumble to dust, but the armor is unharmed.</ansi>
recipe|sporeweave|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">Spores bloom and weave through the fibers, creating a web of mutation that pulses with dormant potential. The armor grows organic and supple.</ansi>
recipe|sporeweave|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The catalyst rejects the binding. The materials crumble to dust, but the armor is unharmed.</ansi>
recipe|stag-hilted-crucible-blade|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You fold and draw the crucible steel into a long blade and carve its grip from a trophy antler. A stag-hilted crucible blade!</ansi>
recipe|stag-hilted-crucible-blade|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The blade cracks in the temper. The crucible steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|stamina-tonic|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You steep the thistle until the liquid turns sharp green. A stamina tonic!</ansi>
recipe|stamina-tonic|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The brew turns sour and you pour it out. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|steel-bone-saw|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You cut and set the teeth, harden the blade and fit the grip. A steel bone saw!</ansi>
recipe|steel-bone-saw|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The teeth crack as you set them. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-bow-saw|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You draw a long steel blade, cut and set the teeth and string it in a hardwood frame. A steel bow saw!</ansi>
recipe|steel-bow-saw|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The blade kinks as you tension it. The materials are ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-buckler|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You shape the steel into a gleaming buckler and set it on a wooden grip. A steel buckler!</ansi>
recipe|steel-buckler|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The steel dishing is uneven and the buckler warps. The materials are ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-cleaver|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You draw out the steel, harden the spine and grind a clean edge. A steel cleaver!</ansi>
recipe|steel-cleaver|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The blade warps in the quench. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-felling-axe|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge a heavy wedge of steel, temper the bit, and hang it on a long hickory haft. A steel felling axe!</ansi>
recipe|steel-felling-axe|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The bit chips in the temper and the head is useless. The steel is lost.</ansi>
recipe|steel-hide-scraper|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge and grind a smooth steel curve and fit two hardwood handles. A steel hide scraper!</ansi>
recipe|steel-hide-scraper|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The blade cracks in the quench. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-ingot|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You fold the iron with coal dust, working it through many heats. A steel ingot!</ansi>
recipe|steel-ingot|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The carbon mix is uneven and the metal becomes brittle. The materials are lost.</ansi>
recipe|steel-lockpicks|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You draw the iron into fine blanks, grind precise tips, and bind them in a tight roll. Steel lockpicks!</ansi>
recipe|steel-lockpicks|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The picks snap during tempering -- the tips are too brittle to salvage. The materials are lost.</ansi>
recipe|steel-longsword|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge the steel into a long, keen blade and wrap the hilt in leather. A steel longsword!</ansi>
recipe|steel-longsword|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The steel cracks along a hidden flaw. The materials are ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-pick|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge a hardened steel head and fit it to a hardwood haft. A steel pick!</ansi>
recipe|steel-pick|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The point snaps in the hardening. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-sickle|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You draw out a thin steel crescent, harden it and fit the haft. A steel sickle!</ansi>
recipe|steel-sickle|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The crescent warps in the quench. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-skinning-knife|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge the steel thin, harden the curved edge, and polish it until it shaves. A steel skinning knife!</ansi>
recipe|steel-skinning-knife|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The edge cracks in the hardening. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|steel-whittling-knife|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You forge a slim steel blade, harden the point and set it in hardwood. A steel whittling knife!</ansi>
recipe|steel-whittling-knife|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The point snaps in the hardening. The steel is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|stillwater-lake-chowder|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You shuck the clams over the pot, soften the root vegetables in the broth, and float the mint leaves in at the last moment. The chowder smells of the lake on a fair morning. Stillwater lake chowder!</ansi>
recipe|stillwater-lake-chowder|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The clams oversteep and the chowder turns grey and stringy. The pot is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|stillwater-pearl-pendant|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You set the dark pearl in a silver bezel and weave the chain fine, finishing with the small clasp. The pearl seems to drink the lamplight as you work. A stillwater pearl pendant!</ansi>
recipe|stillwater-pearl-pendant|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The bezel will not seat right against the pearl, and the wire fights every twist. The materials are ruined; the pearl is unharmed.</ansi>
recipe|stone-stomach|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You carefully extract the venom and neutralize it with thistle. A stone stomach elixir!</ansi>
recipe|stone-stomach|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The venom reacts violently with the thistle. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|swiftfoot-essence|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">The liquid becomes almost weightless in the bottle. A swiftfoot essence!</ansi>
recipe|swiftfoot-essence|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The herbs wilt before the essence can form. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|talon-ring|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You shape a silver band and set the talons to curl around it. A talon ring!</ansi>
recipe|talon-ring|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">A talon cracks as you seat it. The materials are wasted.</ansi>
recipe|tan-leather|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You soak the cured hide in bark liquor, work it soft and stretch it to dry. A leather hide!</ansi>
recipe|tan-leather|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The hide sours in the vat and comes out brittle. It is ruined.</ansi>
recipe|tan-pack-hide|success_actor => <ansi fg="green">You salt the hide, work it soft, stretch it on the rack to dry, and cut the finished leather into strips. Leather strips!</ansi>
recipe|tan-pack-hide|failure_actor => <ansi fg="red">The salt cure fails and the hide sours on the rack. It is ruined.</ansi>
